---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Terms of Use — BVT';
const description =
  'The terms that apply to the BVT Chrome extension and this website, including acceptable use, content rights, third-party services, and disclaimers.';
const lastUpdated = 'November 15, 2026';
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms', href: '/terms/' },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="container-page py-10 sm:py-14">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { name: 'Terms', href: '/terms/' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-600">
          Legal
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">
          Terms of Use
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
          These terms apply to the BVT Chrome extension and this website. By installing or
          using BVT, you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use the extension.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <div class="not-prose mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-amber-950">
        <p>
          <strong>Plain-language note:</strong> BVT is a download tool, not a permission
          slip. A public video can be technically downloadable and still be someone else’s
          copyrighted work. You are responsible for how you use the files.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>1. What BVT is</h2>
      <p>
        BVT is an independent Chrome extension for downloading public TikTok videos,
        batch-selecting videos from supported pages, collecting short drama episodes, and
        exporting selected public metadata to XLSX. It is not affiliated with TikTok,
        ByteDance, or the Chrome Web Store.
      </p>
      <p>
        BVT works with the page you open and the data that page makes available. It does
        not provide a complete TikTok archive, a private-content service, or a server-side
        download service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. License to use the extension</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to these terms, you receive a personal, limited, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable license to install and use BVT for lawful purposes. You may not
        reverse engineer, redistribute, resell, sublicense, or modify the extension except
        where applicable law expressly permits it.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use BVT to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>download, store, or share content you do not have the rights to use;</li>
        <li>bypass login, CAPTCHA, region restrictions, DRM, paywalls, or rate limits;</li>
        <li>harass, stalk, dox, or build profiles of individuals;</li>
        <li>infringe copyright, trademark, privacy, publicity, or other rights;</li>
        <li>distribute malware, automate abusive requests, or interfere with TikTok’s services;</li>
        <li>violate applicable law or TikTok’s terms.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the content you download and for how you use it. BVT does
        not review, approve, or grant permission for any use.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Content rights and third-party terms</h2>
      <p>
        Videos, audio, images, captions, and metadata belong to their respective owners.
        Downloading a public video does not give you the right to republish it, use it in
        advertising, include it in a commercial product, or claim it as your own. Confirm
        the license or permission you need before using a file.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your use of TikTok is governed by TikTok’s own terms and policies. BVT does not
        control TikTok’s availability, page structure, rate limits, or decisions about
        content.
      </p>

      <h2>5. No affiliation</h2>
      <p>
        BVT is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or connected to TikTok or
        ByteDance. "TikTok" and related marks belong to their respective owners and are
        used only to describe the platform the extension works with.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        TikTok changes its pages and endpoints. A feature can stop working after a platform
        update, and BVT may need an update to restore it. BVT does not guarantee that any
        page type, video, episode, or field will remain available.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend, or discontinue features. We may update these terms; the
        "Last updated" date will change when we do. Continued use after a change means you
        accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Pro and third-party payments</h2>
      <p>
        Pro is an in-app purchase that unlocks the full batch workflow. The current plan
        and price are shown in the extension before checkout. Payment processing and
        subscription management are handled by third-party services under their own terms.
        BVT does not receive or store your card details.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pro does not change which videos TikTok makes available and does not grant rights to
        use them. A Pro license may be subject to the limits and terms shown at purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        BVT and this website are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of
        any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular
        purpose, non-infringement, and uninterrupted or error-free operation. Some
        jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of certain warranties, so parts of this
        section may not apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, BVT and its operator are not liable for
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost
        profits, data, files, or goodwill, arising from or related to your use of BVT or
        this website. This includes claims related to downloaded content, platform changes,
        or third-party services.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what the extension reads, which
        network requests it makes, and how local settings and Pro licensing work. It is
        part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these terms, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. This page is a
        practical product notice, not legal advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
